  "method": "the score alone (docs/score_training.md): at every decision point (a game tick with finger movement) the actions none, right and left are each tried by simulation from the real game state (none: straight; a turn: once, then straight; until the harp or a death, the window score); a turn at every lag -4..4 ticks from the decision tick (a lag before it runs from the real state that many ticks earlier, with the live game's commands in between), scored 0.9 times the best lag plus 0.1 times lag 0. The right action is the one with the highest score (a tie goes to none); the model is fitted to pick it (softmax, cross-entropy, Adam, L2), each decision point weighted by the gap between the best and the second-best score. Nothing is taken from the live game's turns",
  "settings": {
   "delta": 4,
   "alpha": 0.9,
   "hidden": 16,
   "fit_steps": 600,
   "adam_lr": 0.01,
   "l2": 0.001,
   "model": "mlp",
   "no_back": true,
   "speed_input": false
  },
  "split": "the games listed in test_games were held out (not trained on): --holdout 0.3 --seed 1 --never-test DavidSnake_InputLab_v1.10.63_2026-10-03_235821.txt,DavidSnake_InputLab_v1.13.66_2026-10-04_003849.txt,zDavidSnake_InputLab_v1.13.66_2026-10-08_130959.txt in tools/simlearn.py split()",
  "objective": {
   "windows": "one at every game tick in which the finger moved: its samples in the tick got 1 dp or more away from where it was at the end of the tick before (or from the touch-down); a resting finger, or none, starts nothing",
   "input": "the finger samples of the first 250 ms from the window's start; then, if David turned, one more turn before his next regular step after the latest turn, which ends the input",
   "run": "after the input David goes straight until he eats the harp or dies",
   "harp": "+1 for eating the harp, whenever it happens (only the first); the run ends there",
   "death": "-0.5 times exp(-(s - 1) / decay), s = steps from the window start to the death, decay by cause; a spear hitting David from the side (flying across the direction of his last step) costs nothing",
   "death_decay_steps": {
    "hit the wall": 1.0,
    "speared": 3.7,
    "ran into the tail": 1.0
   },
   "spears": "recorded throws aimed before the window started (throw tick <= start + 18)"
  },
  "result": "Trained on the score alone (docs/score_training.md), same 70/30 split as MNL1 (53 test games, played with ML-1). Per 1000 windows (every game tick with finger movement) on the test games: window score 149.1 (MNL1 304.4, ML-1 298.9; minus MNL1 -155.3, 90% range -187.7 to -128.8); Final score (tolerance 4, alpha 0.9) 309.8 (MNL1 379.2, ML-1 368.3; -69.4, -89.7 to -52.9). Of the 19266 training decision points a turn scored higher than going straight at 67% (none best at 33%, by a mean gap of 0.13 against 0.4 for turns): a single turn toward the harp's row or column pays whatever the finger did, and the finger-only model learned to turn on most finger movement. Turns on the recorded lift-off flick that killed MNL1, a tick earlier (right-turn score +2.91 at tick 948, +4.01 at 949; MNL1 +0.52 at 949, ML-1 -1.06). Not in the game."
